{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WwqDzF65LMWi5dvgNPvXkg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research project carefully to define three tiers of scenarios for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey facts from the data:\n\n**Completed experiments:**\n- MVP-B classification model: 87.5% accuracy, pass F1=87.1%, fail F1=87.9%\n- Oracle simulation (MVP-A): Per-test advantage exists but concentrates in multi-test instances. T=1 (68.7% of instances) gives minimal advantage (iid: 0.0198, block: 0.1088). Block correlation amplifies advantage significantly.\n- P2P regression rate: ~1% (negative finding - too low for P2P to help)\n\n\n- Total distribution with 5% regression shows negative advantage, but 10%+ regression flips to positive.\n\n**Critical pending experiment:**\n- CWM baseline (PREPARING): This is the make-or-break for Claim 1. The gap between classification performance (87.1/87.9 F1) and generation capability will determine whether the story holds.\n\n**Key constraints:**\n- 68.7% of SWE-bench instances have T=1 (single F2P test), where per-test advantage essentially equals trajectory-level advantage\n- P2P regression rate ~1% means P2P signal is essentially useless in practice\n- Block correlation assumption remains unvalidated empirically\n\nNow I'm mapping out the outcome scenarios. In the best case, CWM generation significantly underperforms classification by 12-17 F1 points, block correlation validates empirically, and repo-level results hold. The median scenario shows a moderate 5-8 point gap with partial block correlation and limited repo-level gains. Worst case is a small or nonexistent gap (≤3 points), making the task reformulation story collapse entirely.\n\nFor trace-then-judge, the best outcome would confirm that formulation matters by showing similar performance to CWM, while the worst case would suggest generation itself isn't the bottleneck. Diagnostic re-repair could yield anywhere from 5-10% improvement in resolve rates at best down to noise-level gains at worst. And repo-level performance on SWE-bench ranges from maintaining >80% F1 in the best case to potentially dropping below 70% in the worst.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the block correlation validation and how to structure the YAML output to capture these scenarios clearly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9574,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9574},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8afbbecf-0345-4692-b472-65f2f49a52f1","uuid":"e3663f0f-ab11-40f9-b695-78bbf297c379"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WwqDzF65LMWi5dvgNPvXkg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Classification reformulation yields clear, large advantage over generation; block correlation validated; repo-level transfers\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"CWM generation model hits token-budget and string-matching failure modes at 4B scale, producing large F1 gap vs classification\"\n      - \"Trace-then-Judge performs closer to CWM than to classification, confirming formulation (not just output simplicity) drives the gap\"\n      - \"Block-correlated error structure empirically validated on trained model predictions\"\n      - \"Repo-level classification maintains ≥80% per-class F1 on SWE-bench-PerTest\"\n      - \"Diagnostic re-repair produces statistically significant resolve rate lift\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cwm_generation_per_class_f1: [68, 76]\n      classification_minus_cwm_gap: [11, 19]\n      trace_then_judge_f1: [72, 78]\n      repo_level_per_class_f1: [80, 86]\n      diagnostic_rerepair_resolve_lift_pct: [5, 10]\n      block_corr_spearman_vs_iid: [0.3, 0.6]\n      per_test_failure_precision: [0.82, 0.90]\n      per_test_failure_recall: [0.78, 0.86]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 完全成立。Headline: \"Classification reformulation achieves 87% F1 vs generation's ~72%, \n      a 15-point gap confirming that execution simulation is better cast as classification than generation.\" \n      三个 claim 全部有实验支撑: Claim 1 有大 gap + trace-then-judge ablation; \n      Claim 2 有 re-repair lift; Claim 3 oracle frontier + 实测 block correlation 互相印证。\n      EMNLP Main 投稿，NLP 角度 pitch 为 \"task formulation matters: \n      classification vs generation as a general LLM capability probe\"。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Classification wins but gap is moderate; block correlation partially holds; repo-level degraded; re-repair signal weak\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"CWM generation model handles simple cases but fails on long outputs, producing moderate F1 gap\"\n      - \"Trace-then-Judge sits between CWM and classification, partially confounding the 'formulation vs simplicity' separation\"\n      - \"Block correlation exists but weaker than simulated; effective T closer to iid than block model\"\n      - \"Repo-level classification degrades to 70-79% F1 due to longer context and cross-file dependencies\"\n      - \"Re-repair shows small positive signal but not statistically significant at n=200\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cwm_generation_per_class_f1: [77, 82]\n      classification_minus_cwm_gap: [5, 10]\n      trace_then_judge_f1: [79, 84]\n      repo_level_per_class_f1: [70, 79]\n      diagnostic_rerepair_resolve_lift_pct: [1, 4]\n      block_corr_spearman_vs_iid: [0.1, 0.3]\n      per_test_failure_precision: [0.75, 0.82]\n      per_test_failure_recall: [0.70, 0.78]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Claim 1 需要降调: 不能说 \"fundamentally simpler\"，改为 \"classification offers a favorable accuracy-efficiency tradeoff \n      at small model scales, with a 5-10 point F1 advantage that may narrow at larger scales.\" \n      Trace-then-Judge 结果模糊需要诚实讨论 confound。\n      Claim 2 从 \"measurable downstream improvement\" 弱化为 \"diagnostic signal quality analysis + \n      suggestive re-repair evidence\"，re-repair 作为 pilot 而非主结果。\n      Claim 3 成为论文最强贡献——oracle frontier 分析 + block correlation 实测提供 decision framework。\n      整体 reframe 为 \"When and Why Per-Test Simulation Helps\"，以 Claim 3 的 characterization 为主轴，\n      Claim 1 的 classification advantage 为支撑。EMNLP Main 仍可投但 Findings 更稳妥。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Classification advantage negligible; per-test signal mostly redundant with trajectory-level; story collapses to analysis paper\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"CWM generation model performs comparably to classification at 4B (gap ≤4 F1 points), possibly because function-level tests are short enough to avoid token-budget issues\"\n      - \"Trace-then-Judge matches or exceeds direct classification, undermining the formulation argument\"\n      - \"Block correlation not observed empirically; errors are closer to iid, reducing per-test advantage to oracle-predicted iid levels\"\n      - \"Repo-level classification below 70% F1, not competitive with execution\"\n      - \"Re-repair shows no meaningful lift; diagnostic signals too noisy to be actionable\"\n      - \"68.7% T=1 dominance means per-test ≈ trajectory-level for most real instances\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cwm_generation_per_class_f1: [83, 87]\n      classification_minus_cwm_gap: [0, 4]\n      trace_then_judge_f1: [84, 88]\n      repo_level_per_class_f1: [55, 69]\n      diagnostic_rerepair_resolve_lift_pct: [0, 1]\n      block_corr_spearman_vs_iid: [0.0, 0.1]\n      per_test_failure_precision: [0.65, 0.75]\n      per_test_failure_recall: [0.60, 0.70]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Claim 1 失败——classification 没有显著优于 generation，\"task reformulation\" 叙事不成立。\n      Claim 2 失败——诊断信号噪声太大，无下游价值。\n      Claim 3 的 oracle 分析成为唯一可回收资产。\n      论文必须重构为 analysis paper: \"Do We Need Per-Test Execution Simulation? An Empirical Investigation\"。\n      核心贡献变为: (1) 系统的 oracle frontier 分析揭示 per-test 优势的严格条件 (T≥2, regression rate ≥10%, block correlation); \n      (2) 实证表明当前 benchmark (SWE-bench) 的 test 分布 (T=1 dominant, ~1% regression) 不满足这些条件; \n      (3) classification vs generation 的 null result 本身有信息量——说明在 function-level 尺度上 generation 并不像\n      CWM debugging 文献暗示的那么困难。\n      这个版本更适合 ICSE 2027 (SE venue, empirical study track) 而非 EMNLP。\n      EMNLP Findings 也可尝试，但需要 reframe 为 \"probing LLM code reasoning: when does task formulation matter?\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9574,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9574},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8afbbecf-0345-4692-b472-65f2f49a52f1","uuid":"a67a4b59-0abc-417a-b62b-a4e638deffbf"}
